{:frontmatter
 {:id "adr-2607060100-kotoba-lang-reverse-domain-rename-batch2"
  :title "ADR-2607060100: kotoba-lang -- reverse-domain external-spec rename, batch 2
          (atproto/ipld/bpmn/cmmn/dmn/ical/mcp/multiformats/vrm)"
  :status "accepted"
  :doc_type "adr"
  :topic "kotoba-lang-rename-batch2"
  :authoritative true
  :last_verified "2026-07-06"
  :authoritative_for
  ["9 kotoba-lang repos renamed to reverse-domain external-spec names: atproto->
    org-bluesky-atproto, ipld->io-ipld, bpmn->org-omg-bpmn, cmmn->org-omg-cmmn,
    dmn->org-omg-dmn, ical->org-ietf-ical, mcp->org-anthropic-mcp,
    multiformats->io-multiformats, vrm->org-vrmc-vrm -- each verified genuine (real
    graph/model/interpreter, not just types) by reading actual README/ADR content before
    renaming, per ADR-2607052300's own caution about overclaiming spec conformance"
   "13 dependent repos' deps.edn updated to the new coordinates: vrm dependents
    (network-isekai, net-babiniku, kami-gen-procedural, kami-gen-ml3d, dance,
    kami-app-character-creator, kami-gen-hybrid), multiformats dependents (prolly-tree,
    kami-nv-compat, checkpointer, ipld-itself), ipld dependents (arrangement, chain
    [formerly commit-dag], kotoba-client, prolly-tree)"
   "3 medium-confidence candidates (json, dag-cbor, openapi) deliberately NOT renamed this
    round -- weaker fit to the org-<body>-<spec> shape (json's README never cites RFC 8259
    by name; dag-cbor is an explicitly partial RFC 8949 profile; OpenAPI Initiative isn't a
    w3/ietf-style formal body)"
   "~40 other repos investigated by the audit and excluded entirely -- the
    card/swift/webrtc/etc 'capability library' family and the RDF/linked-data family all
    self-disclaim full spec conformance in their own README/ADR"
   "3 stale manifest/west.yml entries removed as pure hygiene (gltf/glb/usd) -- these repos
    were already renamed on GitHub to org-khronos-gltf/org-khronos-glb/org-openusd earlier,
    but the old duplicate manifest entries were never cleaned up"
   "two real repo-state surprises caught mid-operation and fixed: (1) a git reset --soft
    mistake on arrangement accidentally reverted an unrelated ADR-citation fix already on
    the true remote tip, caught and fixed with an immediate follow-up commit; (2) commit-dag
    had already been renamed to chain by a separate concurrent session (ADR-2607050800) with
    a real content restructure, detected via a repo-name/content mismatch and fixed via a
    direct GitHub Contents API edit against the real current repo instead of trusting the
    stale local checkout"]
  :related
  ["90-docs/adr/2607052300-kotoba-lang-turn-rt-net-signal-reverse-domain-rename.md"
   "90-docs/adr/2607051200-kotoba-lang-ui-family-rename.md"]
  :supersedes []
  :superseded_by []}

 :problem
 {:source "follow-up audit requested after ADR-2607052300: which other kotoba-lang repos
           have bare names that plausibly port a specific external spec but aren't yet
           reverse-domain named?"
  :investigated
  ["background agent scanned ~1200 non-compat-catalog kotoba-lang west.yml entries, read
    each plausible candidate's actual README/ADR (not name-pattern guessing), reported 12
    candidates at varying confidence + a manifest hygiene issue"
   "owner selected: 9 high-confidence candidates (5 no-dependent, 4 with-dependent) +
    the hygiene cleanup; explicitly did NOT select the 3 medium-confidence candidates
    (json/dag-cbor/openapi)"
   "each of the 9 verified genuine before renaming: bpmn/cmmn/dmn each ship a real
    graph/plan-item/decision-table model plus an interpreter, not just types; vrm's README
    documents a full 1:1 restoration from a deleted Rust crate (17 namespaces, ~2650 lines,
    116 ported test assertions); mcp implements real JSON-RPC method names/error codes at
    the manifest/message layer (no transport -- honest scoping, not a disclaimer);
    multiformats verified byte-identical to real go-ipfs/kubo output"
   "multiformats renamed before ipld since ipld itself depends on multiformats --
    dependency-order care, same principle as always fixing dependents before renaming the
    next node up the graph"]
  :risk "same as ADR-2607052300: a repo name overclaiming spec conformance it doesn't have
         is worse than a boring bare name"}

 :decision
 {:renames
  [{:old "atproto" :new "org-bluesky-atproto" :spec "AT Protocol (Bluesky)" :dependents []}
   {:old "ipld" :new "io-ipld" :spec "IPLD DAG-CBOR (tag-42 link discipline)"
    :dependents ["arrangement" "prolly-tree" "chain (formerly commit-dag)" "kotoba-client"]}
   {:old "bpmn" :new "org-omg-bpmn" :spec "BPMN 2.0 (OMG)" :dependents []}
   {:old "cmmn" :new "org-omg-cmmn" :spec "CMMN 1.1 (OMG)" :dependents []}
   {:old "dmn" :new "org-omg-dmn" :spec "DMN 1.4 (OMG)" :dependents []}
   {:old "ical" :new "org-ietf-ical" :spec "iCalendar RFC 5545 (IETF)" :dependents []}
   {:old "mcp" :new "org-anthropic-mcp" :spec "Model Context Protocol (Anthropic)"
    :dependents ["kotodama-mcp"]}
   {:old "multiformats" :new "io-multiformats"
    :spec "multiformats (multihash/CID), verified byte-identical to real go-ipfs/kubo output"
    :dependents ["prolly-tree" "kami-nv-compat" "checkpointer" "io-ipld (itself)"]}
   {:old "vrm" :new "org-vrmc-vrm" :spec "VRM 1.0 (VRM Consortium)"
    :dependents ["network-isekai" "net-babiniku" "kami-gen-procedural" "kami-gen-ml3d"
                 "dance" "kami-app-character-creator" "kami-gen-hybrid"]}]
  :deliberately_not_renamed
  {:medium_confidence ["json (RFC 8259 not cited by name)"
                        "dag-cbor (explicitly partial RFC 8949 profile)"
                        "openapi (OpenAPI Initiative isn't a w3/ietf-style formal body)"]
   :excluded_family ["card/swift/webrtc/banking/securities/treasury/insurance/logistics/
                      retail/labor/phone/ip/pkg/groot/cnc/fea/giemon capability-library
                      family -- self-disclaim 'models records, not wire format'"
                     "rdf/sparql/turtle/n-quads/did/vc/activitypub/activitystreams/
                      rdf-canon/shacl/json-ld -- each self-disclaims full conformance"]}
  :manifest_hygiene
  {:what "removed 3 stale west.yml entries (gltf/glb/usd) pointing at nonexistent local
          paths -- already renamed on GitHub to org-khronos-gltf/org-khronos-glb/
          org-openusd earlier, old manifest entries never cleaned up"
   :cause "gen-west-manifest.bb's --entry flag only adds/replaces, never deletes -- same
           caveat noted in ADR-2607051200 and ADR-2607052300"}
  :execution
  {:steps ["gh repo rename x9, GitHub preserves redirects"
           "local checkout moved + remote retargeted x9"
           "13 dependent deps.edn updates, each its own single-purpose commit"
           "manifest/repos.edn: 9 :path-overrides + 9 :extra-projects updates, API
            single-entry commit"
           "manifest/west.yml: 9 new + 9 removed + 3 stale removed, surgical diff against
            GitHub tip via API (whole-file gen blocked by 4 unrelated pre-existing
            pin-drift repos: browser/cssom/dom-gpu/htmldom, not this batch's concern)"]
   :mistakes_caught_and_fixed
   ["network-isekai/net-babiniku had real unrelated uncommitted WIP (a live-streaming
     broadcast feature) -- committed ONLY deps.edn in each, left the WIP files exactly as
     they were"
    "arrangement: git reset --soft left a stale README.md line staged (pre-fix ADR citation
     2607050600 vs the tip's corrected 2607050700), accidentally reverting that fix on push
     -- caught by inspecting the pushed commit's diff, fixed with an immediate follow-up
     commit, verified git diff against remote showed zero difference afterward. Corrected
     procedure for all subsequent repos: `git checkout <true-tip> -- .` (resets both index
     AND working tree) before reapplying the one-line edit"
    "quad-store: already merged into arrangement by an earlier, unrelated rename
     (ADR-2607050700) -- detected via matching remote-tip SHAs between two supposedly
     different local checkouts, confirmed via gh api; left the stale local dir alone, no
     separate action needed since arrangement's own fix covers it"
    "commit-dag: already renamed to chain by a separate concurrent session
     (ADR-2607050800) with a real content restructure -- detected via repo-name/content
     mismatch on diff, fixed via direct GitHub Contents API edit against the real current
     repo (chain), then resynced the local directory name"
    "kotodama-mcp's fetch showed '(forced update)' -- verified via gh api compare
     (ahead_by:2, behind_by:0) it was a pure fast-forward, not a real force-push, per the
     CLAUDE.md shallow-clone false-positive pattern, before proceeding"]}}

 :consequences
 {:no_behavior_change "name-only renames + mechanical deps.edn coordinate updates; internal
                       Clojure namespaces (vrm.parse etc.) unchanged -- repo name and
                       namespace name are independent concepts (ADR-2607051200 precedent)"
  :dependents_updated "13 dependent repos correctly reference the renamed coordinates"
  :scope_discipline "json/dag-cbor/openapi and ~40 other investigated-and-excluded repos
                     intentionally left alone this round"
  :process_reinforcement "two real repo-state surprises reinforce standing practice
                          (CLAUDE.md, git-cleanup-conflict skill): always fetch and diff
                          against the true remote tip, never assume a shared checkout's
                          local HEAD is current, verify the actual pushed commit's diff
                          before moving to the next repo -- especially with git reset
                          --soft, which does not reset the working tree or catch stale
                          index entries"}

 :alternatives []}
